<section class="copy-section copy-offer" id="assessment" aria-labelledby="assessment-heading"><div class="wrap copy-body"><div class="section-title"><h2 id="assessment-heading">First, establish your threat model and risk assessment.</h2></div><div class="section-detail">
<p><strong>Private Exposure Assessment &#xB7; &#x20AA;3,600 including VAT &#xB7; Typically four hours</strong></p>
<p>We begin with your circumstances and the information you need to protect. Toza examines relevant apps, devices, accounts, access arrangements and digital traces to develop your personal threat model: the ways information could become exposed and the consequences that matter to you.</p>
<p>The Assessment covers one main phone and one PC, iPad or second phone, with relevant identities, accounts and data access. You receive a specific risk assessment, priorities and ordered next steps in the practical summary. This sets the plan for hardening, new accounts where needed, recovery and operational changes.</p>
<p>If we identify urgent exposure, Toza will address what can safely be fixed within the visit&apos;s agreed scope, with your approval. The visit completes the agreed intake, mapping, diagnosis and approved urgent first aid; you receive the summary whether or not you continue.</p>
<p><a href="/en/private-exposure-assessment.html">The first paid visit in detail</a></p>
